# Extra environment for start-chromium.sh. Installed to /etc/pioneer-tv/chromium.env.
# The window size comes from board.env; only put overrides here.
#
# Extra Chromium flags:
# PIONEER_TV_CHROMIUM_FLAGS="--force-device-scale-factor=1"
#
# GPU flags. Default: GPU compositing and rasterisation with zero-copy uploads.
# Set to an empty string to let Chromium decide on its own.
# PIONEER_TV_GPU_FLAGS=""
#
# Video decoding: "software" (default) or "hardware". The Pi's decoder wedges
# on resolution changes, which is what makes adaptive players pause; software
# H.264 costs well under a core and never stalls.
# PIONEER_TV_VIDEO_DECODE=hardware
#
# PIONEER_TV_PROFILE=/home/pi/.pioneer-tv/chromium
